[h1]Living Fellows 0.26.28 - Camp life playtest[/h1]
[list]
[*]Base Watch keeps the camp active through a companion's second local view while you travel. Remote status and defense orders use the squad radio channel.
[*]Fishing expeditions choose confirmed loaded shoreline banks instead of houses. The leader needs a rod and bait; equipped teammates can fish too.
[*]The Chef prepares meals from real ingredients and tools. Blocked supplies, fridges and stoves now report a stalled job instead of trapping the Chef on duty.
[*]Camp workers can find marked storage, books, beds, washing water, cleaning and tidying work, and leader check-ins on connected floors. Building and indoor shelter routes retain the native stair path.
[*]Companions can drink from reachable sinks and wells, watch TV on another camp floor, and use a powered camp radio during downtime. They can tune a station, take a free seat, listen and comment on broadcasts.
[*]Tired companions sleep for several game hours. Chair sitting varies from 25 to 85 game minutes.
[*]Floor and wall planning no longer throws the Build 42 container-list error. Base job failures appear under Stalled jobs with Retry and Cancel controls.
[*]Base policy controls and stock summaries are easier to read. Camp, stair and furniture recovery received further fixes.
[/list]

This is a playtest build. Fishing destinations require loaded shoreline. Corpse dragging still cannot use stairs. Please report logs and screenshots when an animation, path or job stalls.
